Pipeline Considerations:
1. Before Batching (Per Individual Post): The "Hard Block" Filter
Before you run a vector search or group your 10 posts, pass each raw post through a very fast, local text check (like a simple Python Regex keyword scanner).
2. After Batching (Per Cluster): The "Sentiment & Alignment" Filter
Now, your pipeline runs its vector search on those 8 clean posts and successfully groups them into 2 distinct trend clusters (Trend A has 3 posts, Trend B has 5 posts).
Outcome: If Trend A is a positive shift toward plant-based eating, it passes. If Trend B turns out to be a sarcastic meme mocking animal welfare, you drop the entire cluster at once before it ever hits your UI dashboard.

Final Thought of pipeline:
Cronjob: Request pipeline on subreddits /new and types every hour, use UNIQUE keyword for deduplication, and this polls regularly, assumes no webhook as assumes a large number of posts
Ingestion: Your scheduled background script polls the target communities (e.g., fetching a raw batch of 10 posts from Reddit).
Normalization: FastAPI uses Pydantic to instantly strip platform-specific keys and serialize the payload into a unified JSON format.
The Queue Connection Point: The normalized posts are enqueued directly into your Redis Queue (Arq/Celery). The heavy processing steps below are now handled asynchronously by background workers, keeping your main app completely non-blocking.
Pre-Batch Check: The Redis worker runs a lightning-fast local regex pass or other checks to drop explicit gore, abuse trigger words, or blocked content before computing embeddings.
Batching into Trends: Your clean posts hit your database via Supabase pgvector to dynamically cluster them into distinct trend buckets based on semantic similarity. It must explicitly select and link the top 5 most representative or highest-engagement raw posts (IDs, text content, and platform links) to that trend record. This ensures that when Phase A saves the trend to Supabase, the UI has the exact five examples ready to render.
Post-Batch Check: The worker evaluates the compiled trend clusters as single units, running sentiment rules to omit hostile, sarcastic, or anti-advocacy angles.
Human in the Loop Trend Explainer: Generating a low-cost AI summary of a trend's relevance to animal rights to help human users decide whether to trigger full content generation. 
Cybersec Check: The system sanitizes the final trend payload, applying prompt-injection defenses and structural isolation rules before generating the query.
Gemini Generation Call: The system dispatches the context to the Gemini API, forcing a strict structured JSON output to map out tailored advocacy captions, hashtags, and text variants.
Revalidation: The pipeline performs a fast, zero-cost programmatic check on the text output to guarantee it aligns with core boundaries before saving the final trend to your Supabase tables and evaluating using OpenPaws models and displaying it on simple dashboard.
